**Palette gaps [G3]:** the master palette (226 colours) has thin skin ramps. It has no pale elf skin, no tiefling red/violet skin, and few light warm tones (known since trial B09/B10). Proposal: add a `pal_skin_hair` block of ≤24 colours, Owner-approved, to the palette authority.

## 7. Worked example — human man, medium look (all 6 states)
This is the v1 fighter example adapted to the medium look (sword + shield). The dark red brigandine stands in for the human race-theme tabard colour [C]. Only the S-direction prompts are shown; animations run in all 8 directions with the facing phrases in §4.1.
Values:
- Race: H=42, W=18, C=44, CS=56, heads 3.2, head 13 / torso 13 / legs 16, top row 2, feet row 43, centre column 22.
- Anchors: dy_hand = 15, dx_hand = 10; shoulders at dy 29, belt at dy 16.
- Seeds: crc32 of `human_m_medium_{stage}`, attempt 0.
- Size refs: scale_chart.json@f3af0b11 CHARACTER_HUMAN_ADULT + strip@5ce5cefe.
- Palette: `pal_human_medium.png`.
- Slot IDs: `CH.HUMAN.MEDIUM.M.<STATE>.<ANIM>.<DIR8>.F<n>`.

**Stage 1 — Base** (`create-character-v3`, image_size 44×44, low top-down, mannequin, single color outline, medium detail, enhance_prompt false, no_background true)
```
human man in a mail shirt with short brown hair and a determined face, wearing a steel mail shirt, a dark red padded brigandine vest with a brown leather belt, brown wool trousers and brown leather boots, a longsword sheathed at his left hip and a round wooden shield slung on his back, empty hands.
Low top-down view. Figure 42 px tall and 18 px wide at the shoulders in a 44x44 px canvas: top of head on row 2, feet on row 43, body centred on column 22.
Head 13 px, torso 13 px, legs 16 px (3.2 heads tall); shoulders at 29 px above the feet, belt at 16 px above the feet, hands hanging at 15 px above the feet, 10 px left and right of centre.
Colours: skin #dc906b with shadow #b06a4b and highlight #cfb38d; hair #734f2d, shadow #49331e, highlight #a2713f; steel mail #8c9da9, shadow #55636f, highlight #ede9de; dark red brigandine #b5280d, shadow #6d1109, highlight #cf8667; leather belt and boots #734f2d, shadow #49331e, highlight #a2713f; wool trousers #674a35, shadow #423023, highlight #91694a. At most 32 colours.
Rounded steel pauldrons 5 x 4 px on each shoulder; brigandine vest from the shoulders to the belt with 1 px rivet dots #ede9de; scabbard 14 px long and 2 px wide at the left hip from (+8,17) to (+11,4), leather #734f2d with a gold #f7c03d crossguard 5 px wide showing at the top; round oak shield 12 px across on his back, oak #834a34 with a 1 px iron rim #606568, showing 2 px beyond each shoulder in the front view.
1 px dark outline tinted from each area's own shadow colour, no anti-aliasing, no dithering. Light from the top left, shadows on the lower right.
```
Base animations (`characters/animations` v3, one call per direction, all 8 directions):
- `description` = the base text with the facing phrase added after "empty hands" (e.g. "…, empty hands, facing the viewer."). `color_image` = base_palette, `force_colors` true, `keep_first_frame` false.
- **Idle** (frame_count 4): `standing idle breathing in 4 frames: the chest and shoulders rise 1 px and fall back; the arms sway 1 px; the feet stay planted. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the sheathed longsword stays exactly 14 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.`
- **Walk** (frame_count 4): `walking in place in 4 frames: frame 1 left foot forward, frame 2 passing with both feet under the body and the head 1 px higher, frame 3 right foot forward, frame 4 passing; the arms swing opposite to the legs by 2 px. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the sheathed longsword stays exactly 14 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.`

**Stage 2 — Attack State** (`create-character-state`, override_frame_size 56×56, use_color_palette_from_reference true, state_name "Attack")
```
Change to an attack pose with the longsword: he has drawn the longsword and holds it raised over his right shoulder ready for a rising diagonal slash, with the round shield on his left forearm in front of his chest. The longsword is 18 px long (blade 14 px, crossguard 5 px wide, grip 3 px), the blade 2 px wide steel #8c9da9 with a 1 px #ede9de edge, held in his right hand at (-9,22) and angled 45 degrees from vertical up and away from his body; the shield is round, 12 px across, centred on his left forearm at (+8,20), oak #834a34 planks with a 1 px iron rim #606568 and a 3 px steel boss #8c9da9. Feet 8 px apart. Keep his face, hair, body proportions, outfit, colours and 1 px self-tinted outline exactly the same; the figure stays 42 px tall with the feet on the same baseline and centred on the same column. Everything stays inside a 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
Attack animation (v3, 6 frames, on the Attack State):
```
rising diagonal sword slash in 6 frames: frame 1 ready pose with the sword over the right shoulder, frames 2-3 wind-up drawing the sword back and down to the right hip, frame 4 strike sweeping the blade up and across the body to the upper left, frame 5 follow-through with the blade high on the left and the shield tucked in, frame 6 return to the ready pose. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the longsword stays exactly 18 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
**Stage 3 — Cast State** (override 56×56, palette-from-reference true, "Cast")
```
Change to a spellcasting pose: he raises a small holy emblem overhead in his left hand with the arm straight up, his right palm open and held forward at chest height. The emblem is a 4 x 4 px gold #f7c03d sun disc with shadow #a2713f on a 1 px leather cord #734f2d, held at (+6,40); no glow. The longsword stays sheathed at his left hip and the shield stays on his back as in the base. Keep his face, hair, body proportions, outfit, colours and 1 px self-tinted outline exactly the same; the figure stays 42 px tall with the feet on the same baseline and centred on the same column. Everything stays inside a 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
Cast animation:
```
raising a holy emblem in 6 frames: frame 1 ready holding the emblem at the chest, frames 2-3 lifts it overhead and opens the right palm, frame 4 thrusts the emblem 2 px higher, frames 5-6 lowers it back to ready. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the emblem stays exactly 4 px wide, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
**Stage 4 — Ranged State** (override 56×56, palette-from-reference true, "Ranged")
```
Change to a ranged attack pose: he holds a light crossbow level at his right shoulder in both hands and aims straight ahead, the left hand under the stock and the right hand at the trigger. The crossbow is 12 px long and 14 px wide at the bow arms, stock oak #834a34 with shadow #583224, bow arms iron #606568, string 1 px #c8c3b7, held at (-4,28); the bolt is 8 px long, shaft #a2713f with a 2 px steel tip #8c9da9. The shield stays on his back and the longsword sheathed as in the base. Keep his face, hair, body proportions, outfit, colours and 1 px self-tinted outline exactly the same; the figure stays 42 px tall with the feet on the same baseline and centred on the same column. Everything stays inside a 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
Ranged animation:
```
shooting a light crossbow in 6 frames: frame 1 ready aiming, frames 2-3 steadies the aim and squeezes the trigger, frame 4 releases with the string snapping forward and the bolt leaving, frames 5-6 lowers the crossbow and reloads a bolt. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the crossbow stays exactly 12 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
**Stage 5 — Down State** (override 56×56, palette-from-reference true, "Down")
```
Change to lying unconscious on the ground on his back, body stretched horizontally with the head to the viewer's left, arms loose at the sides, eyes closed; the body is 42 px long and at most 20 px tall from the ground, lowest pixel on the feet baseline, centred on the same column; the round shield lies flat beside his hip and the longsword lies on the ground beside him, 18 px long. Keep his face, hair, outfit, colours and 1 px self-tinted outline exactly the same. Everything stays inside a 48 x 48 px box.
```
Down animation (v3, 6 frames, on the Down State, `custom_start_frame` = base rotation of that direction, `end_frame` = Down rotation):
```
collapsing in 6 frames: frame 1 standing, frame 2 knees buckle, frame 3 falls to the knees, frame 4 tips backward, frame 5 hits the ground, frame 6 lying still; the longsword falls beside the body. The lowest pixel ends on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the longsword stays exactly 18 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
**Stage 6 — Work State** (override 56×56, palette-from-reference true, "Work")
```
Change to a working pose: he stands at a small anvil and raises a smith's hammer in his right hand, the left hand holding a glowing bar on the anvil with tongs. The hammer is 8 px long (haft 6 px oak #834a34, head 3 x 2 px iron #606568), held at (-8,26); the anvil is 12 px wide and 7 px tall, iron #606568 with shadow #3a3e42 and highlight #7c8389, standing on the ground at (+6,0); the bar is 6 x 1 px #f26018. The longsword stays sheathed and the shield on his back as in the base. Keep his face, hair, body proportions, outfit, colours and 1 px self-tinted outline exactly the same; the figure stays 42 px tall with the feet on the same baseline and centred on the same column. Everything stays inside a 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
Work animation (loop):
```
hammering at an anvil in 6 frames as a loop: frames 1-2 raises the hammer above the shoulder, frame 3 strikes the bar on the anvil, frames 4-6 lifts back to the start; the anvil stays fixed in place. The feet stay on the baseline, the head and body keep their size, the hammer stays exactly 8 px long, and nothing leaves the 48 x 48 px box around the feet.
```
Note: the fire-orange bar (#f26018) is a new colour for the medium-look palette. Either add it to `pal_human_medium` or drop the glow [C, O3].

## 8. Open items needing Owner decision
- **O1 Height conflicts [G1].**
  - Dwarf: scale_chart 36 px (34–38) vs size_classes 32 px (28–35).
  - Elf: scale_chart 43 (42–46) vs size_classes 39 (33–44).
  - This draft uses scale_chart (Owner-named). Pick one; the other file should be fixed.
- **O2 Cast gestures per look** (§5): one gesture per look now serves every class wearing it (e.g. a heavy-armor paladin and a heavy-armor fighter share the hilt-up gesture; a light-armor warlock and a light-armor rogue share the open-palm thrust). Confirm the five gestures.
- **O3 Glows in States.** Is a small glow (≤3 px) allowed in cast states, or are all spell visuals separate FX layers? A glow needs `use_color_palette_from_reference` false for that state, or a palette entry.
- **O4 Action frames.** Frame class MEDIUM/SMALL is 48×48. Big weapons (greatsword 22, staff 30) are designed to fit inside the 48 box, but swings may clip. Should action clips be allowed a 64×64 (or 48×64 TALL_MEDIUM) frame? Default: fit into 48, clip = retry.
- **O5 Base carries the weapon sheathed/slung with empty hands** (best for idle/walk, matches the L09 look), and the weapon appears in hand only in the Attack state. Confirm.
- **O6 Default weapons, ranged weapons and work tools per look** (§5, all [C]). The attack/ranged visual follows the **look**, not the weapon actually wielded (a wizard stabbing with a dagger still shows the staff). One Work State per look shows one tool; colony jobs (mining, farming, smithing) will not match it unless the job visuals come from shared overlays or props [C].
- **O7 Prompt enhancement off.** L09's preferred look was made with enhancement ON. First production call: A/B base human with `enhance_prompt` false vs true (2×2 gens).
- **O8 Small races [G5]:** halfling 21 px / gnome 25 px at the v3 minimum canvas of 32 (the model tends to fill the canvas). Turn on the readability floor (26–28 px)? The first gnome and halfling are test calls.
- **O9 Widths [G6]:** size_classes copies the human width (14–22) to the small races and to dragonborn/half-orc with status PROPOSED. Suggested widths: halfling 12, gnome 13, half-orc 20, dragonborn 20.
- **O10 Head ratios [G4]** for races the chart lacks (half-elf 3.2, half-orc 3.0, tiefling 3.1, dragonborn 3.3, gnome 2.4, halfling 2.3): proposed.
- **O11 Palette [G3]:** add a ≤24-colour skin/hair block (pale elf, tiefling red/violet, more warm light skins) to the master palette. Also: one skin tone per race sprite, or 2–3 palette-swap variants (0 gens, local) to match faceset people [G2].
- **O12 Dragonborn ancestry [G8]:** one bronze sprite plus palette swaps for the other ancestries (0 gens)?
- **O13 Tiefling horns and tail [G7]:** counted inside the 42 px height (proposal) or on top?
- **O14 Budget** (§9).
- **O15 Robe vs unarmored** for units wearing no armor. Proposal: robe if the highest-level class is a caster (bard, cleric, druid, sorcerer, warlock, wizard) [C: or only wizard/sorcerer/warlock]; unarmored otherwise.
- **O16 Class in the portrait.** "Class shows in the portrait": per-class portrait art would multiply the faceset presets by class; proposal: a class badge/frame on the portrait and the class name/icon in the selected-unit panel, with no extra generation [C].
- **O17 Children and elders** are not in the 90. Proposal: child and elder unarmored looks per race × sex as a later add-on [C].
- **O18 8-direction sheet layout** for the RMMZ 8-way movement plugin (row order, walk playback).
- **O19 Unarmored classes** (barbarian, monk) look like commoners on the map; accepted per "classes may look alike" unless the Owner wants an exception.
- **O20 Shields:** only the medium look shows a shield; a heavy-armor unit with a shield, or a light-armor unit with a sword, still shows its look default.

## 9. Generation estimate (v2: 90 sprites, all animations in 8 directions)
Per sprite (first pass, measured prices where known):
| Item | Calls | Gens |
|---|---|---|
| Base (v3, C ≤ 64) | 1 | 2 |
| States (5 × 20, CS ≤ 84) | 5 | 100 |
| Base idle + walk (2 anims × 8 dirs × ~1) | 16 | 16 |
| State animations (5 × 8 dirs × 1–2) | 40 | 40–80 |
| **First pass** | 62 | **158–198** |
| Retries (base 30 %, states 20 %, anims 25 %) | | +1 / +20 / +14–24 → **~193–243** |

**All 90:** first pass **14,220–17,820 gens**; with retries **~17,400–21,900**; plus the O7 / O8 test calls (~10–30) and the first crowd/battle test (one race × both sexes × 1–2 looks, ~400–500). 8-direction animation roughly doubles the animation share versus the v1 4-direction figure (56–96 vs 28–48 per sprite); States are unchanged because the State API always returns 8 rotations.

For comparison: v1 (216 class sprites, 4-direction animations) was 28,080–32,400 first pass; the 288-sprite plan with 8-direction animations would have been ~45,500–57,000. The v2 total is inside the ~40k the Owner accepted. Current balance is 9,741 against a hard stop of 9,740, so there is **no usable budget** until a top-up.

Cost levers (Owner choice):
- **(a)** Down and Work as v3 animations on the base (`end_frame` poses) instead of States: saves 40 per sprite, about 3,600 in total.
- **(b)** Share one Down State per race × sex across looks: not recommended (the outfit must match).
- **(c)** Diagonal directions are free in States, since the State API always returns 8.
- **(d)** No mirroring (handed weapons), so no savings there.

## 10. Manifest and files
- Prompts are generated by code from §4 with slot values from `pixellab/prod/slots/{race}.json` (incl. the race-theme block) and `{look}.json` (to create). Every call is logged per §3.
- Outputs go to `pixellab/prod/{race}/{sex}_{look}/` (raw, post, sheets, contact); packed clips are named by slot ID.
- This standard supersedes the class-sprite parts (now character-sprite parts; §3.0 still says 216 per class and needs a pointer update) of `DEUS_GENERATION_RECIPES.md` §3.0/§3.1 where they differ.
